  full_example | skill | all   | 0.95 | example, full, tags, conformance

::node[full_example]
->[:role=skill]
->[:scope=all]
->[:keywords=example, full, tags, conformance]
->[:requires=hello]
::dense
full_example|all-tags|conformance fixture exercising every node-level block type
::full
This node exercises every tag type defined in the ObjectGraph spec.
It is used by the conformance suite to verify that a parser populates
all fields correctly from a single source file.
::steps
1. Read the ::dense block to get the compressed summary.
2. Read the ::full block for complete details.
3. Check ::warning before executing any side effects.
4. Execute the ::steps in order.
5. Validate outcome against ::assertion conditions.
::warning
Never use this fixture in production — it is a conformance test only.
::note
This fixture deliberately includes every optional block type.
::example
A parser that reads this file and omits any block fails the conformance check.
::assertion
dense_present: the ::dense block must not be empty
steps_ordered: steps must be returned as an ordered list
warning_present: the ::warning block must not be empty
::edges
->[:requires] hello
->[:calls] external-system
::traverse
priority=high
entry=full_example
depth=1
